        "url": "https://www.metafilter.com/215186/A-severe-weight-and-balance-headache",
        "content_text": "An airplane cannot just take off and soar to its final cruising altitude on a long-range flight. When an airliner first takes off, its fuselage is heavily laden with thousands of gallons of jet fuel required to cross an ocean or reach a distant continent. <a href=\"https://simpleflying.com/airbus-a321xlr-often-stuck-climbing-1st-few-hours-flight/\">Step climbing</a> is a dynamic operational technique designed to maximize fuel efficiency by matching an aircraft's altitude to its changing weight over the course of a long-haul journey.",
