        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/11/12/apple-sports-adds-ufc-events-with-real-time-stats-and-results/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/11/apple-sports-ufc.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Apple continues to expand the appeal of its free Sports app, which focuses on delivering real-time sports scores and stats, across many different sports. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Today, Apple is adding UFC into the mix, so MMA fans can track the fights live through the unified Apple Sports experience. </p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"apple-sports\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1078470\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/11/12/apple-sports-adds-ufc-events-with-real-time-stats-and-results/#more-1078470\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
